<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Morgan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1635–<a href="/years/1688">1688</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sir Henry Morgan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Morgan was a Welsh privateer based at Port Royal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, who led raids on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-america">Spanish America</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portobelo">Portobelo</a> in 1668 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maracaibo">Maracaibo</a> in 1669. In 1671 he crossed the isthmus and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-city">Panama City</a>, which was rebuilt on a new site. He was later knighted and served as lieutenant governor of Jamaica.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-morgan.jpg" alt="Henry Morgan" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexandre Exquemelin, Piratas de la America (1681) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morgan,Henry.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
